    "updated_at": "2023-05-18T05:50:00Z",
    "body": "Thanks @bathos \r\n\r\nYour reply in the other repo was good. This was good too. Much appreciated.\r\n\r\nLearned about `window.welcomeMessage` when I came across `document.all`. Pretty scary imo haha!\r\n\r\nWhat I meant by \"What about a document.forms for elements with an id?\" is me asking if there has been any consideration for a similar property on `document` that exposes all elements with an id? Since somebody somewhere long ago found good reason to make `document.forms` and it was apparently good enough to not get deprecated, then why isn't there a property exposing all elements with an id, like `document.elements.welcomeMessage`?\r\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
